    "file": "R:\\Music\\Vombatus\\Tombeau\\02 Ouverture (The Parade).mp3",
    "text": {
      "TXXX": "lyrics-eng\u0000[Call | a single distant unaccompanied brass call, alone, echoing]\n[Ouverture | slow ceremonial 4/4, heavy dotted rhythms, harpsichord and strings, D major, grand]\n[Procession | full orchestra at its most stately, everything correct and polished]\n[Turn | the dotted rhythm tightens, strings sharpen, something underneath is wrong]\n[Fugue | fast 6/8 at 168 BPM, distorted guitars enter with the fugue subject, double-kick]\n[Unison | harpsichord and lead guitar play fast runs in exact unison, virtuosic, relentless]\n[Too Fast | tempo pushes, the playing gets tighter and harder, D minor, strained]\n[Outro | the ceremonial dotted rhythm returns, worn out and slower, ending on a bleak D minor chord] | comment\u0000made with suno; created=2026-09-16T21:12:14Z; id=0537527b-c287-4ba9-a3e7-a8ec5cc98d38",
      "TIT2": "Ouverture (The Parade)",
      "TCON": "Baroque Progressive Metal",
      "TPE1": "Vombatus",
      "TPE2": "Vombatus",
      "TALB": "Tombeau",
